    <rigor>FULL</rigor>
    <rigor-reason>Highest-blast-radius task in the project — a new association rung in shared `Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/` that decides which of 7 core records an email files onto. A wrong match MISFILES email (the #1 trust-killer per research). Value-based reverse lookup, defensive catalog reads, reinforcement-gated auto-file, per-message query-cost budget. BFF-touching + `.cs` in the shared engine → code-review + adr-check at Step 9.5 UNCONDITIONALLY; publish-size + CVE + `/conflict-check` required.</rigor-reason>
    <parallel-group>P2-assoc</parallel-group>
    <parallel-safe>false</parallel-safe>
    <model-tier>opus</model-tier>
    <model-tier-reason>Architectural, high-blast-radius association correctness with genuine ambiguity boundaries (bare-numeric reinforcement, multi-entity disambiguation, defensive dirty-catalog reads). §8.5 assigns `opus` to high-blast-radius/architectural work; this is the canonical case.</model-tier-reason>
    <effort>xhigh</effort>
    <fr-refs>FR-01, NFR-08</fr-refs>
  </metadata>

  <prompt>
    Add ONE new deterministic association rung to the EXISTING ladder in `src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/` that extends identifier-based matching from matter-only to all 7 core record types (matter, project, invoice, work assignment, budget, service request, report card). Clone the shape of `ExplicitReferenceRung.cs` (rung 0) + `ThreadContinuityRung.cs` (rung 1) and implement `IAssociationRung`. This EXTENDS the ladder — MUST NOT add a second engine or a second regarding mechanism (ADR-045 / ADR-024).

    The rung is **catalog-driven and value-based** — NO numbering scheme lives in code (binding MUST rule):

    1. **Roster from `sprk_recordtype_ref`** — read the per-record-type `sprk_regardingfield` + `sprk_regardingrecordnumberfield` (the number field to reverse-look-up against) from the catalog. Read it **DEFENSIVELY** using task 001's typo/anomaly map (some `sprk_regardingfield` values have typos; the `contact` row is anomalous) — normalize/guard so a dirty row never produces a wrong field name or a false match. Onboarding a new tenant must require ONLY `sprk_recordtype_ref` config, no code change (FR-01 acceptance).
    2. **Extract identifier-shaped tokens** from subject + body (the tokens that look like record numbers, e.g. `PRJT.10001.01`, `CMRCL-441482`, `INV-002`). Extraction is deterministic/pattern-based — do NOT hardcode per-entity numbering; extract candidate tokens broadly, then match by VALUE.
    3. **Value-based reverse lookup** — for each candidate token, exact-match its VALUE against the number field of each of the 7 record types (via the catalog roster). A match is a record whose number field EQUALS the token value. The numbering scheme is NEVER decoded in code; matching is pure value equality against Dataverse.
    4. **Reinforcement-gated auto-file (per C-1)** — a **bare-numeric identifier alone NEVER auto-files** (needs sender/participant/thread reinforcement). An explicit, well-formed identifier match is a rung-0-class result; a bare-numeric token needs reinforcement before it can be treated as auto-fileable. Emit the rung result + status; the actual auto-file-vs-Suggested narrowing is finalized by task 021, but THIS rung MUST emit the signals 021 needs (rung level + reinforcement flag) and MUST NOT itself auto-file a bare-numeric-only match.
    5. **Multi-entity → `Ambiguous`** — if a token value matches records of MORE THAN ONE entity type (or multiple records), resolve to `Ambiguous`, never a guess.
    6. **Cost budget (NFR-08)** — gate the reverse lookup to NOT-yet-resolved emails only; cache catalog + lookups; report the per-message query count. MUST NOT run the reverse lookup on already-associated emails.

    Add seam + unit tests covering the acceptance set below. This is the rung ONLY — the auto-file policy narrowing (rung 0+1 vs 2/3) is task 021; the report-card `RegardingFieldMap` entry is task 010 (a dependency for writing a report-card match).
  </prompt>

  <role>
    Spaarke BFF engineer for the Communication Association Engine — authority on `Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/` and the deterministic association ladder. Fluent in ADR-045 (extend the ladder, add one rung — never fork), ADR-024 (one regarding mechanism, resolver-only write), the `sprk_recordtype_ref` catalog contract, value-based (not scheme-based) matching, §10 BFF Hygiene, §11 Component Justification, and NFR-08 query-cost discipline. You never encode a numbering scheme in code; you read the catalog defensively; you never let a bare-numeric token auto-file alone.
  </role>

  <goal>
    A new catalog-driven identifier rung exists in the ladder (mirroring rung 0/1, implementing `IAssociationRung`): it extracts identifier-shaped tokens from subject/body, reverse-looks-them-up by VALUE against the 7 record types' number fields (roster from `sprk_recordtype_ref`, read defensively per the 001 typo/anomaly map), and emits a match + status + reinforcement signals. A well-formed explicit identifier associates to the correct record across all 7 types; a bare-numeric token alone NEVER auto-files; a token matching multiple entities resolves to `Ambiguous`; the reverse lookup runs only on not-yet-resolved emails, is cached, and the per-message query count is reported. No numbering scheme in code; onboarding a tenant needs only `sprk_recordtype_ref` config. Build clean; seam + unit tests green; existing association tests stay green; publish-size delta ≈0 + no new HIGH CVE; `/conflict-check` run before the PR.
  </goal>

  <context>
    <background>
      The shipped ladder deterministically associates matter numbers only (`ExplicitReferenceRung`, rung 0) and inherits thread associations (`ThreadContinuityRung`, rung 1). FR-01 extends this to all 7 core records via a catalog-driven rung: numbering schemes vary per tenant and per record type, so the rung MUST NOT hardcode them — it reads the roster (regarding field + number field per record type) from `sprk_recordtype_ref` and matches candidate tokens by VALUE. This keeps tenant onboarding to catalog config only.

      §11 Component Justification: (1) **Existing** — `ExplicitReferenceRung` matches matter numbers only (grep-confirmed); no rung matches project/invoice/work-assignment/budget/service-request/report-card numbers. (2) **Extension** — this is ONE new rung class mirroring rung 0, reusing `IAssociationRung`, the catalog, and the resolver write path; no new engine, no new regarding mechanism. (3) **Cost-of-doing-nothing (concrete)** — without it only matter numbers deterministically associate; project/invoice/etc. never auto-match and G-1 fails (success-criterion 1). Named contract failure, not "future flexibility."

      The dirty-catalog risk is real (spec §Dependencies; 001 note): some `sprk_regardingfield` values have typos and the `contact` row is anomalous. Reading the catalog naively would produce a wrong field name (query error) or a false field mapping (misfile). The rung MUST guard against this using the 001 map. Misfiling is the #1 trust-killer (design research) — hence bare-numeric-never-auto-files and multi-entity→Ambiguous are non-negotiable guardrails.
    </background>
    <relevant-files>
      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/Rungs/ExplicitReferenceRung.cs (rung 0 — CLONE its shape: token extraction + catalog read + value match)</file>
