      <file>src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/Services/Communication/Engine/AssociationStatusMapper.cs + AutoFileGate.cs (downstream C-1 narrowing — task 021 consumes this rung's level + reinforcement signals)</file>
      <file>projects/email-communication-intelligence-r1/notes/001-operator-schema-verification.md (the verbatim `sprk_recordtype_ref` roster + the defensive-read typo/anomaly map — CONSUME)</file>
    </relevant-files>
  </context>

  <constraints>
    <constraint source="FR-01">Scope: extract identifier-shaped tokens from subject/body; exact-match VALUES against each of the 7 record types' number fields; roster + fields from `sprk_recordtype_ref`. An email quoting `PRJT.10001.01` / `CMRCL-441482` / `INV-002` associates to the correct record; onboarding a tenant needs ONLY `sprk_recordtype_ref` config.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project (numbering out of code)">Scope: NO numbering scheme in code — matching is pure value equality against the catalog-named number field. MUST NOT decode/parse any per-entity numbering format to decide the target entity.</constraint>
    <constraint source="C-1 / FR-03">Scope: a bare-numeric identifier alone MUST NOT auto-file (needs sender/participant/thread reinforcement); emit the rung level + reinforcement flag that task 021 uses to gate auto-file vs `Suggested`. This rung MUST NOT itself auto-file a bare-numeric-only match.</constraint>
    <constraint source="FR-01 (disambiguation)">Scope: a token value matching more than one entity type (or multiple records) resolves to `Ambiguous` — never a guess.</constraint>
    <constraint source="spec §Dependencies">Scope: read `sprk_recordtype_ref` DEFENSIVELY using the 001 typo/anomaly map — normalize/guard so a typo'd `sprk_regardingfield` or the `contact` anomaly never yields a wrong field name or a false match.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-08">Scope: gate the reverse lookup to not-yet-resolved emails; cache the catalog + lookups; report the per-message query count. MUST NOT run the reverse lookup on already-associated emails.</constraint>
    <constraint source="ADR-045 / ADR-024">Scope: extend the ladder (add ONE rung implementing `IAssociationRung`); write via the existing resolver/`RegardingFieldMap`. MUST NOT add a second engine or a second regarding mechanism.</constraint>
    <constraint source="NFR-04">Scope: the rung MUST be best-effort — a lookup failure or dirty-catalog row MUST NOT fail the capture/enrichment path; degrade to no-match/Suggested, never throw into the capture path.</constraint>
    <constraint source="project §10">Scope: BFF Hygiene — load `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md`; state the Placement Justification in the PR; report publish-size delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (expected ≈0); no new HIGH CVE; update tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` + seam tests (ADR-038); `/conflict-check` before the PR (shared `Services/Communication/Engine/`).</constraint>
  </constraints>

