  <steps mode="directional">
    <step order="1">Read `.claude/constraints/bff-extensions.md` §F/§G + §11 + task 001's note (verbatim roster + defensive-read typo/anomaly map) + `DATA-ACCESS-DECISION-CRITERIA.md` before designing.</step>
    <step order="2">Read `ExplicitReferenceRung.cs`, `ThreadContinuityRung.cs`, `IAssociationRung.cs`, `RegardingFieldMap.cs`, `AssociationStatusMapper.cs`, `AutoFileGate.cs` to fix the rung contract, the result/status shape, how the ladder orders rungs, and the exact signals `AutoFileGate`/`AssociationStatusMapper` need from this rung for 021's C-1 narrowing.</step>
    <step order="3">Characterize the existing ladder with a green test baseline (existing association behavior MUST stay green after the new rung is inserted).</step>
    <step order="4">Implement the new rung: (a) deterministic token extraction from subject/body; (b) defensive catalog read (roster from `sprk_recordtype_ref` via the 001 map, guarding typos + the `contact` anomaly); (c) value-based reverse lookup against the 7 number fields, gated to not-yet-resolved emails + cached; (d) emit result with rung level, match, status, and the reinforcement flag; (e) bare-numeric-only → NOT auto-fileable (needs reinforcement); (f) multi-entity/multi-record → `Ambiguous`; (g) best-effort (never throw into the capture path). Count per-message queries.</step>
    <step order="5">Insert the rung into the ladder at the correct precedence (mirroring how rung 0/1 register); confirm `RegardingFieldMap` (incl. the task-010 report-card entry) can write each of the 7 matches.</step>
    <step order="6">Write seam + unit tests in `tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/` + `tests/integration/seam/**`: (a) a well-formed identifier for EACH of the 7 record types associates to the correct record; (b) NEGATIVE — a bare-numeric token with NO reinforcement is NOT auto-filed (rung emits not-auto-fileable); (c) NEGATIVE — a token value matching two entity types resolves to `Ambiguous`; (d) NEGATIVE — a dirty/typo'd `sprk_recordtype_ref` row does NOT produce a wrong-field query or a false match (defensive read); (e) cross-tenant numbering works with only `sprk_recordtype_ref` config (no code change); (f) the reverse lookup does NOT run on an already-associated email + the per-message query count is asserted (NFR-08); (g) a lookup failure degrades to no-match, not an exception into the capture path (NFR-04).</step>
    <step order="7">Run `dotnet build src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/` + `dotnet test tests/unit/Sprk.Bff.Api.Tests/ --filter Communication` + the seam tests; confirm existing association tests still pass.</step>
    <step order="9.1">Run `dotnet publish -c Release src/server/api/Sprk.Bff.Api/ -o deploy/api-publish/`; report compressed size + delta vs ~49.63 MB baseline (expected ≈0).</step>
    <step order="9.2">Run `dotnet list package --vulnerable --include-transitive` — confirm no new HIGH-severity CVEs.</step>
    <step order="9.5">FULL-rigor quality gates: `code-review` on the diff (focus: no numbering scheme in code, defensive catalog read, bare-numeric-never-auto-files, multi-entity→Ambiguous, NFR-08 cost, NFR-04 non-fatal, one-mechanism/ADR-024); `adr-check` against `spec.md` (FR-01, ADR-045/ADR-024, NFR-08, NFR-04). Address Critical findings; cite bff-extensions Placement Justification + §11.</step>
