  <escalation>
    <trigger>Identifier-extraction ambiguity that the deterministic guards do NOT cleanly resolve — e.g. a numbering format that is genuinely undecidable by value alone, a `sprk_recordtype_ref` anomaly beyond the 001 map (a row whose number field cannot be read defensively), or a case where "bare-numeric never auto-files" + "multi-entity → Ambiguous" would still risk a misfile. Misfiling is the #1 trust-killer; a genuine ambiguity boundary is a legitimate STOP (root §6), not something to guess past. Surface the specific token/record-type + the guard that fails and request a human decision on the disambiguation rule before shipping.</trigger>
  </escalation>

