  <acceptance-criteria>
    <criterion testable="true">A well-formed identifier for EACH of the 7 core record types (matter, project, invoice, work assignment, budget, service request, report card) associates to the correct record via value-based reverse lookup against the catalog number field.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">No numbering scheme is hardcoded in code — matching is pure value equality against the `sprk_recordtype_ref`-named number field; a new tenant's numbering works with only catalog config (no code change).</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a bare-numeric identifier token with NO sender/participant/thread reinforcement is NEVER auto-filed by this rung — it emits a not-auto-fileable result + the reinforcement flag 021 consumes.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a token value matching more than one entity type (or multiple records) resolves to `Ambiguous`, never a guessed single match.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NEGATIVE: a typo'd `sprk_regardingfield` or the `contact`-row anomaly in `sprk_recordtype_ref` does NOT produce a wrong-field query or a false match — the catalog is read defensively per the 001 map.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NFR-08: the reverse lookup runs ONLY on not-yet-resolved emails, is cached, and the per-message query count is reported and asserted; it does NOT run on already-associated emails.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">NFR-04: a lookup failure or dirty-catalog row degrades to no-match/Suggested and NEVER throws into the capture/enrichment path.</criterion>
    <criterion testable="true">Extends the ladder (ONE rung implementing `IAssociationRung`, writes via the existing resolver/`RegardingFieldMap`) — no second engine, no second regarding mechanism; existing association tests stay green; publish delta ≈0 vs ~49.63 MB; no new HIGH CVE; `/conflict-check` run before the PR.</criterion>
  </acceptance-criteria>

  <notes>
    The single most important property is no-misfile: bare-numeric-never-auto-files and multi-entity→Ambiguous are non-negotiable guardrails (misfiling is the #1 trust-killer). Depends on 001 (the defensive-read roster + typo/anomaly map) and coordinates with 010 (the report-card `RegardingFieldMap` entry that lets a report-card match be written). Blocks 021 (which finalizes the C-1 auto-file narrowing using this rung's level + reinforcement signals), 024 (RI-confidence reads this rung's agreement), 030/040/042. If a genuine ambiguity boundary appears, fire the escalation trigger — do NOT guess past it.
  </notes>

